  "arithmetic": {
    "input_interpretation": "Every decoded JSON float is treated as its exact IEEE-754 binary64 value; this review bounds only the subsequent complex128 algebra, not CKKS/decode error.",
    "high_precision_method": "math/big.Rat exact rational arithmetic over the binary64 inputs; algebraic identity and first-order remainder are evaluated without intermediate rounding.",
    "first_order_model_residual": "U = P1 - d1*C. U is the Stage2 operation-residual change r2a-r2b and is not a floating-point closure error or a claim about a specific CKKS primitive.",
    "full_identity_closure": "E = P1 - (d1*C + (r2a-r2b)); the exact-rational identity is zero for every slot when all terms use the same decoded binary64 inputs.",
    "unit_roundoff": "u=2^-53 for round-to-nearest binary64; the old gate used 2^-52 as u and gamma_64 over only final small terms.",
    "complex_add_sub_bound_l1": "For L(z)=|Re(z)|+|Im(z)|, each complex add/sub absolute error is bounded by u*(L(a)+L(b)), absent overflow/underflow.",
    "complex_multiply_bound_l1": "The componentwise two-product-plus-add/sub complex multiply has L1 error \u003c= gamma_2*L(a)*L(b), gamma_2=2u/(1-2u), absent overflow/underflow.",
    "full_closure_bound_derivation": "Per slot: eP=u(L(Yon)+L(Yoff)); eD=u(L(Xon)+L(Xoff)); ePred=L(C)*eD+gamma_2*L(Dfl)*L(C); eA=gamma_2*L(Xon)*L(C)+u(L(Yon)+L((Xon*C)fl)); eB is analogous; eDiff=u(L(rAfl)+L(rBfl)); eRhs=ePred+eA+eB+eDiff+u(L(predfl)+L(diffFl)); Ebound=eP+eRhs+u(L(P1fl)+L(rhsfl)). The exact rational L1 envelope is compared against the L1 norm of the complex128 closure residual.",
    "bound_assumptions": [
      "The error bound follows the existing operation order in computeFixedSigmaAblationPropagation: subtract P1 and d1, multiply d1*C and X*C, subtract r2a/r2b, subtract their difference, add the RHS, then close with the final subtraction.",
      "All input and intermediate values are checked finite; captured magnitudes are normal-range or exact zero, so the standard relative roundoff model's overflow/underflow exclusions hold.",
      "L1 bounds are conservative upper bounds on complex Euclidean magnitude; the bound is operation-derived, not a tuned multiplier or a change to the original gate."
